{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent\/consentgating"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}],"role":"article","title":"Consent Gating","roleHeading":"Article"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Guides","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/DefiningEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow"],"anchor":"Guides"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each event type names the purpose it is collected for, its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"consentCategory"},{"text":", which is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".analytics"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"unless its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event(consent:)"},{"text":" says otherwise. Give the tracker a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Consent"},{"text":", which the app updates as the user","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"decides, and an event reaches a destination only once its category is granted:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["@Event(consent: .advertising)","struct AdClicked {","    var campaign: String","}","","let consent = Consent([.analytics: .granted])","let tracker = Tracker(consent: consent)","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(","    to: ConsoleDestination(),","    ConsoleDestination().accepting(.advertising)",")","tracker.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\"))          \/\/ delivered: analytics is granted","tracker.track(AdClicked(campaign: \"spring\"))  \/\/ held: advertising is undecided","consent.grant(.advertising)                   \/\/ delivers the held AdClicked"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A tracker given no consent delivers every event."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Undecided, granted and denied","anchor":"Undecided-granted-and-denied","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A category is undecided until the app grants or denies it. While it is undecided, its events are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"held in memory, not written to a store, up to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"heldRecordLimit"},{"text":" records (1,000 by default) across","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every category, the oldest dropped first when the hold is full. Granting delivers them in the order","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"they were tracked, before anything tracked after the grant. Denying drops them. Events tracked while","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"their category is denied are never collected.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"grant"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deny"},{"type":"text","text":" return at once: they record the decision, and the tracker’s worker releases or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"drops what it held. Every drop of a record that was held or kept is reported on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"consent.dropReports"},{"type":"text","text":" as a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ConsentDropReport"},{"type":"text","text":" as it happens, so none is lost silently. Held"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"records are lost if the app ends first."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Records that a store recovered from an earlier run are gated again as the tracker starts. They are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"held outside the bound, since the store still keeps them, and the store forgets each one that is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"denied.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Destinations","anchor":"Destinations","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A destination receives every category the consent lets through, unless "},{"code":"accepting(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" narrows it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to the categories it serves, as the second destination above takes only advertising."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating"},"abstract":[{"text":"Deliver an event only once the user grants the purpose it is collected for.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/SessionsAndStandardContext":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/sessionsandstandardcontext","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Stamp every event with its session and with the app, device, system, locale and network it was tracked on."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext","title":"Sessions and Standard Context","role":"article","type":"topic","kind":"article"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/AutomaticTracking":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/automatictracking","role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Automatic Tracking","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Track screen views, control activations and the app’s lifecycle without a call at each place they happen."}]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/DefiningEvents":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/definingevents","abstract":[{"text":"Derive an event’s conformances and schema from its declaration with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"text":", and constrain which values its properties may hold.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/DefiningEvents","title":"Defining Events","role":"article","type":"topic","kind":"article"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Typed analytics events for Swift, delivered in batches to any number of destinations."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent","title":"Traffluent","role":"collection","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/SamplingEvents":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/samplingevents","abstract":[{"text":"Keep a seeded fraction of the events a tracker tracks, event by event or a whole session at once.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents","title":"Sampling Events","role":"article","type":"topic","kind":"article"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TrackingPlanWorkflow":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingplanworkflow","role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Exporting and Checking a Tracking Plan","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tell the people and services that read your events what each event holds, and hear about a change that would break their data before it ships."}]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/PersistingRecords":{"title":"Persisting Records","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so a record the app tracked survives the process ending."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords"}}}